  "body": "## What changed\n\nImproves the lower bound on C_47 from 1.70311* (#321) to **1.7032090736***. Adds its row and reference to `constants/47a.md`, updates the README table cell and \"Recent progress\". Markdown only. Stacked on #321, which adds the 1.70311 row; we will rebase once it is merged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Witness: a periodic atomic measure with 63 atoms per cell, in the input format of Tomar's checker.\n- Exact ratio: `3132581668909806427917067970204393210052649/1839223215401194968772738622942534413844480` = 1.70320907363..., rounded down. The bound uses Tomar's Lemma 6.2, following Lin, which we did not re-derive.\n- Three computations return this same fraction: Tomar's unchanged `check_exact2.py`, the search's own evaluator, and a separately written `verify.py`. `verify.py` was written after reading Tomar's checker and uses the same enumeration and the same sweep with a segment tree, so it checks the implementation, not the mathematics, and is not an independent method.\n- Certificate: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24022791.\n  SHA-256 `construction.json`: `5f7a8d9dfc88514c24995fd81b085b7c05ab4e2b9e43dcb923e48b3b6a7e310b`\n  SHA-256 `verify.py`: `9517816987ac146890e11b927dbb90a06e477e2f77dbc208c1ed6337f7ebd9d6`\n\n## Context\n\n| Step | Lower bound | Gain |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [Lin2026] | 1.6855099933 | |\n| [Tom2026] | 1.7027237335* | 1.02% |\n| #321 | 1.70311634* | 0.023% |\n| this PR | 1.7032090736* | 0.0054% over #321 |\n\nThe measure descends from the #321 measure by atom moves, insertions and removals, so this continues that line rather than being a new structure. As a baseline, plain single-atom hill-climbing from #321 (moves and mass changes only, no insertions) reached at best 1.7031626 over four one-hour runs, about half of this gain. A longer or richer polish may do better.\n\n## Use of AI\n\nThe measure was found by [SCiEL](https://sciel-rsi-cpil.github.io/), a recursive self-improvement (RSI) system built on cultural transmission, running an open language model (Qwen3.8-27B) that writes and refines search programs scored by the exact ratio.\n",
  "state": "open",
